  "authoringDirection": "Whole principal Hongu sanctuary ensemble: all16 vertices of main building57008547, both separate6-point inner gate roofs57008548/57008551 and whole24-point outer worship hall373238591. Preserve the main building, flanking low sections and south spur, two inner roofed gates and full outer hall/wings with open passages. Original four wood-palisade traces remain thin intrinsic architectural fences with their native gaps. Steep copper-gray Shinmei gables, exposed wood posts/boards/brackets, projecting ridge ends, forked chigi and cylindrical gold-ended katsuogi. Exclude the separate Kagura-den, Doyoden, treasure hall, other shrines, whole wooded religious parcel, natural ground/trees/people/flags/signs/crest art/sacred interiors. Keep all16/6/6/24 original physical plan vertices; retain native gaps/open yards and thin fence traces, no whole precinct or courtyard slab. Original main16 partitions: central taller steep gable, two flanking lower sections and south spur; exact partitions/heights bounded. Inner gates are distinct steep gables with genuine open passages under the roof, not opaque box doors covering the whole opening. Outer24 worshiphall has complete wings and projecting central roof/passage, bounded hidden front details. Use muted dark copper roof/layered fascia, warm weathered unpainted timber boards/round posts/trusses/visible gable overhang/ridge/paired forked chigi/cylindrical katsuogi with small gold ends. Fence rows coarsen at distance while retaining native trace/gaps. Do not copy Kamon/letters or infer main architecture from published Kagura/Doyoden images. Freeze independent384m129x129field at fixed south approach before geometry; no flatten/fitting/reacquisition, actual forest/urban approach contact unverified.",
